WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.040
- Have you ever had a
neighbor that was so bad

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.710
you just wished you could sue them

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:05.580
and get them to move
out of the neighborhood.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.480
- I want you out!

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.310
- Well, today we're going to indulge

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:11.240
in your neighbor-suing fantasy

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.820
with some of the worst neighbors
that have ever existed.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.590
On the matter of next door neighbors,

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:18.617
English author G.K
Chesterson famously quipped,

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:20.647
"The Bible tells us to love our neighbors,

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:22.107
"and also to love our enemies;

00:00:22.107 --> 00:00:25.400
"probably because generally
they are the same people."

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.010
Clearly, Mr. Chesterton had
some bad neighbors himself

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.520
or knows some jaded real estate lawyers.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.210
But it's an all too relatable sentiment

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:34.810
because few parts of life
inspire more acrimony

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:37.130
and generate more attorney's fees

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.210
than drawn out fights between neighbors.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.790
Which might explain why neighbor
disputes seem to make up

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:44.743
90% of sitcom plot lines.

00:00:44.743 --> 00:00:45.900
- Ew!

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.100
- What?

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.774
- Ugly naked guy's taking
his turkey out of the oven.

00:00:49.774 --> 00:00:50.607
(audience laughing)

00:00:50.607 --> 00:00:52.520
- And it's all too common
that neighbors are presented

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.040
with straightforward
solutions to their problems,

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:57.320
but due to pride, animosity, or both,

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.730
they choose to dig in their heels

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.210
and incur tens of thousands,

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:01.890
if not hundreds of thousands of dollars,

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:03.110
in legal fees instead,

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:05.720
which is bad for neighbors,
but great for lawyers.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.070
So let's start with property
lines and boundary disputes.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:09.700
Perhaps the most common neighbor dispute

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.560
is when one property owner discovers

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.310
that his or her neighbor has built a fence

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:15.620
or other structure that
crosses the boundary line,

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.930
which creates a cause of
action known as encroachment.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:20.650
And most of the time such
encroachment is unintentional.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:23.200
Boundary lines can date back
decades or even centuries,

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.700
and as time passes, successor
neighbors can forget

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.690
exactly where the original lines are.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:30.350
When a road or structure,
or even a pile of rocks,

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.300
extends into a neighbor's property,

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:35.770
this also creates a cause of
action for continuing trespass.

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:37.460
And to get the court to order the removal

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:38.720
of these infringing structures,

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:41.580
an individual can file a
common law action for ejectment

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.450
to prove that the individual
has the sole right

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:45.400
to possess the property
that is being encroached

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.780
or trespassed upon.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:48.620
But ultimately, the
simplest way to resolve

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.700
boundary disputes is for
the parties to get together

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.830
and pay for a lot line adjustment

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.220
that moves the official property lines

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:55.950
to match the neighbors'
current boundaries.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:57.850
But if every neighbor
could resolve disputes

00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.510
in a calm and mature fashion,

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:02.180
there'd be no need for this
video about nightmare neighbors.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:05.000
For example, when Gabriel
Brawn of Bangor, Maine

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.380
discovered that his property line

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.780
included one half of
his neighbor's garage,

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.940
he then decided to take
matters into his own hands

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.980
by sawing the garage in half.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.320
I mean, from a legal perspective,

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.790
absolutely the wrong way
to handle that dispute,

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:18.650
but that is some tremendously precise

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:19.760
construction work right there,

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.610
some real Matt Risinger stuff.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:25.000
- We'll see you next
time on The Build Show!

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:25.970
- Here's the background.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:28.130
In 2012, Gabriel and
his wife, Tracy Brawn,

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:29.700
moved to Gabriel's childhood home

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.370
and peacefully coexisted with
their neighbor, Steve Ritter.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:35.220
But things changed after
Mr. Ritter died in 2016

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.280
and Steve's widow, Theresa Laythe-Ritter,

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.970
and their son Blake took
ownership of the property.

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:43.010
Gabriel described Blake
as, "A terrible neighbor,"

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.300
who he alleged had late night parties

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.330
and was rude to the
Brawns and their children.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:49.300
The dispute escalated in April 2020

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.800
when the Brawns put down wood chips

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.510
near the previously
established boundary line

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.680
to allow a tractor to travel downhill

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:56.300
to clean up downed tree limbs.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.420
Blake responded to this
act by planting a stake

00:02:58.420 --> 00:02:59.960
in the ground where the chips were placed

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.700
and demanding that
Gabriel remove the chips

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.743
from what he claimed
was the Ritter property.

00:03:03.743 --> 00:03:06.440
Gabriel then hired two
different land surveyors

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:07.480
to check the boundary lines,

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.740
who both concluded that
half of the Ritter's garage

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:11.230
was on the Brawn property.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:13.030
Blake asked Gabriel for the opportunity

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:15.130
to remove his father's
ashes from the garage,

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:17.810
but Gabriel claims his
neighbor began throwing trash

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:19.940
and smashing glass and throwing bureaus

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.110
in front of the lawn.

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:23.340
The next day, Gabriel,
who works in construction,

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.290
sawed the garage in half.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.900
Following widespread media coverage,

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.350
the Ritters sued the
Brawns and the surveyors,

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:30.770
the purported crane operator,

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:32.270
and even media organizations

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:34.070
that reported on this controversy.

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:35.560
Shortly after this lawsuit was filed,

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:38.380
the judge ordered the
Brawns to set aside $150,000

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:39.860
to pay future damages,

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.440
noting the Ritters would
likely prevail at trial.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:44.900
Gabriel, who was representing
himself and his wife

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:46.250
instead of hiring a lawyer,

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.930
now can see that he could
have handled this better,

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:50.737
noting that he would have liked to,

00:03:50.737 --> 00:03:53.990
"Have seen a better resolution
to the dispute myself."

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:56.060
I mean, sure, Brawn
could have hired a lawyer

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:58.010
to negotiate a redrawing
of the boundary lines,

00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.740
kind of like how the
Ritters had hired lawyers

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:01.000
to litigate their case.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.640
But instead of doing the sensible thing,

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.770
Gabriel clearly had been guided
by one animating principle:

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:10.040
How would a cartoon neighbor
act in this situation?

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:12.840
- There. Now we live in
completely separate houses.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:15.010
I don't ever have to look at you--

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:17.500
- Now here's some #NotLegalAdvice.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:19.150
If you get into a legal dispute,

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:20.460
it's a good idea to hire a lawyer

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.550
instead of trying to
fix everything yourself.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:25.037
That's why in the legal
profession we have a saying:

00:04:25.037 --> 00:04:27.620
"Only a fool would have
himself as a client."

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.990
And given the likelihood of
the self-represented Brawns

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:32.170
losing to the lawyered-up Ritter clan,

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:35.500
this is just another
example of brain over brawn.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.750
Yeah! Nailed it!

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.880
Come for the legal analysis,
and stay for the terrible puns.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.440
Now let's talk about easements.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.330
Anyone who makes the leap from
being a renter to a homeowner

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:46.090
does so with the intention
of having property

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:48.210
that is truly their own and no one else's.

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:49.970
However, what a lot of
people may not realize

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.980
is that most homes come with easements,

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:54.920
which expressly grant certain
rights to allow third parties

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:56.410
to enter your land and use your property.

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:58.350
And when there are
disputes about strangers

00:04:58.350 --> 00:04:59.460
coming onto your property,

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:01.610
that's where you can run into problems.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.080
Easements grant individuals,
companies, or the government

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.370
the right to use or access
another individual's property

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:07.350
for limited purposes.

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:10.490
These easement rights typically
include physical access,

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:11.420
like the right of way,

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:13.610
or utility easements that
allow public entities

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.630
to install telephone poles, gas lines,

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:16.690
and other infrastructure.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:19.460
And parties can also
obtain negative easements,

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:21.950
which gives a holder of the
right to require a neighbor

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.100
to do or not do specific things,

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:26.840
such as preventing an owner
from blocking the neighbors view

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.170
or obstructing water flow.

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:29.020
And of these easements,

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:30.900
the most common one is
the driveway easement

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:31.920
in which a neighbor has the right

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:34.630
to use the property owner's
driveway to access his land.

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:35.900
You wouldn't think that a driveway

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.830
could be a source of such conflict,

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:40.870
but then you've never lived
next to Minnie Driver.

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:43.610
I mean, I haven't either,
but judging by her feud

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.080
with her 70-something-year-old
disabled neighbor

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:48.710
over a driveway easement,
I'm not sure I want to.

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:50.540
Here's what happened in that case.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:53.020
In September 2014, the
"Good Will Hunting" star

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:54.940
moved in next door to Daniel Perelmutter,

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:57.010
a 74-year-old disabled Army vet

00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:59.370
and heart transplant survivor
who walks with a cane.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:01.850
Problems began immediately
that December when Perelmutter

00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:04.560
began building an ultra
modern home on his property

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:06.290
bordering on a shared driveway.

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:08.350
Perelmutter claimed that Driver
had gone to great lengths

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:10.210
to block access to his driveway easement

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:12.010
that leads to several parcels of land,

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:13.370
including Driver's property.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:15.010
Driver further blocked the easement

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:16.630
with the installation
of an electronic gate

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:18.200
to protect her from the paparazzi.

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:20.460
This was originally done with
the blessings of Perelmutter

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:23.090
and his wife, but Driver
allegedly changed the code

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:24.820
and disabled the manual gate switch

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.370
after construction began.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:27.700
In November 2015,

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.670
Driver obtained a
temporary restraining order

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:32.107
against Mr. Perelmutter claiming that he,

00:06:32.107 --> 00:06:35.090
"Cursed us and blew smoke
in my children's faces,"

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:37.970
and otherwise put the Driver
family in fear of their lives.

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:39.820
Perelmutter denies this misconduct.

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:42.290
In 2016, the Perelmutters
sued for trespass,

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:43.520
private nuisance, assault,

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:45.890
and intentional infliction
of emotional distress.

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:47.887
He claims in his suit that driver threw,

00:06:47.887 --> 00:06:49.557
"Baby food jars filled with black paint

00:06:49.557 --> 00:06:50.930
"against the walls of his home."

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:52.810
Driver denied Perelmutter's allegations

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:53.940
and claimed that he was the one

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:55.600
who was deliberately
blocking the driveway,

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.370
as Perelmutter had installed a new wall

00:06:57.370 --> 00:07:00.700
that narrowed the driveway
down from 20 to 14 feet wide.

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:03.430
In November 2016, Driver went
to Los Angeles Superior Court

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:05.970
in Perelmutter was
found guilty of contempt

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:08.420
for shrinking the driveway
easement with his wall.

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:10.770
He was ordered to do 10
hours of community service

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:14.230
and pay $200,000, plus
Driver's attorney's fees.

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:17.640
To avoid jail, Perelmutter
reluctantly tore down that wall,

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:19.270
but continued to lash out at Driver

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:22.194
in a January 2017 court
hearing alleging she,

00:07:22.194 --> 00:07:23.927
"Perjured herself in every way

00:07:23.927 --> 00:07:25.747
"with her testimony of complete lies,

00:07:25.747 --> 00:07:28.600
"putting on a performance
worthy of an Oscar winner."

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:30.250
Perelmutter then file a new lawsuit

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:32.740
accusing Driver of outrageous
and malicious behavior,

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:34.340
screaming insults and obscenity at him,

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:36.210
driving at him in her car,

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:38.440
causing $20,000 worth of
damage to his property,

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:41.680
and threatening to have his
construction workers "deported."

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:42.710
Perelmutter also claimed

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:44.700
that after winning the
prior lawsuit against him,

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:46.767
he videotaped Driver, "Gloating,

00:07:46.767 --> 00:07:49.617
"telling him that she
was glad he got F'ed,

00:07:49.617 --> 00:07:52.990
"and wishing that he would
lose everything as a result."

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:54.860
However, it's clear
Perelmutter hasn't been

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:56.700
the most diplomatic of neighbors either,

00:07:56.700 --> 00:08:00.207
previously telling the
dailymail.com about Ms. Driver,

00:08:00.207 --> 00:08:01.817
"She won and I hope she spends

00:08:01.817 --> 00:08:03.970
"every dollar on chemotherapy."

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:04.850
Jesus.

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:06.140
And after three years of fighting,

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:07.300
the neighbors finally reached

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:08.660
a confidential settlement agreement

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:11.250
for all claims in April 2018.

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:13.160
The presiding judge, Rita Miller,

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:14.820
had expressed disappointment in court

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:16.830
that the two couldn't
resolve their differences

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.857
without litigation, noting with a chuckle,

00:08:18.857 --> 00:08:22.190
"The heart of the case is who's
richer than who, I guess."

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:23.230
So my Legal Eagles,

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:25.100
the big takeaway here
is that if you disagree

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:26.680
with the scope of an easement,

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:29.400
it's best to try talking
things out with your neighbor.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.920
Unless, of course, you're very angry

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:33.350
and have hundreds of thousands
of dollars for legal fees,

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:36.760
in which case my telephone
line is always open.

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:39.560
But that takes us to private
and public nuisances.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:41.140
One of the most common
complaints people have

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:43.140
about their neighbors is
that they are annoying,

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:46.110
and most of the time being
annoying is not a crime,

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:47.800
even though it definitely should be.

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:48.790
But at a certain point,

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:50.870
did you know that you can be so annoying

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:53.250
that it actually violates the law?

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:55.650
Well, this brings us to
our next legal concept,

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:56.800
nuisance law.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:58.650
Individuals who own or occupy real estate

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:00.420
have a common law right to what's called

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:02.060
quiet enjoyment of their property,

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.790
meaning that they have the right to use

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:06.250
and enjoy their premises in
peace without interference

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:08.270
from the surrounding
neighbors or landlord.

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:10.110
A person commits the tort of nuisance

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:12.360
when a person in
possession of real property

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:15.040
engages in an activity that
significantly interferes

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:17.000
with user enjoyment of another's property,

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:18.860
or otherwise affects the
health, safety, welfare,

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:20.980
or comfort of the public at large.

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:22.050
So when you hear stories

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:23.620
about nightmare celebrity neighbors,

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:25.770
those claims typically
fall under nuisance law.

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:27.270
For example, in 2011,

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:30.070
eccentric filmmaker and foot
enthusiasm Quentin Tarantino

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:32.207
brought a private nuisance
lawsuit against his neighbors,

00:09:32.207 --> 00:09:33.810
"True Blood" creator Alan Ball

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:35.660
and his partner Peter Macdissi,

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:38.007
alleging their macaw parrots emitted,

00:09:38.007 --> 00:09:40.257
"Ear splitting shrieks and screams

00:09:40.257 --> 00:09:42.310
"for seven to eight hours a day."

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.352
Tarantino argued that the
macaws subjected him to,

00:09:44.352 --> 00:09:47.520
"Obnoxious pterodactyl-like screams,"

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:50.047
which have, "robbed Mr.
Tarantino of the ability

00:09:50.047 --> 00:09:51.610
"to find peace in his home."

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:53.600
And if you think
Tarantino is exaggerating,

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:56.387
this is what a macaw call sounds like.

00:09:56.387 --> 00:09:58.130
(macaw screeching)

00:09:58.130 --> 00:09:59.220
(image beeping)

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:01.360
But sometimes the nuisance
doesn't affect one person,

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:02.810
it affects the public at large.

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:04.410
And there was a public nuisance case

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:07.310
relating to the Sriracha
factory in Irvine, California.

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:09.430
The city of Irvine filed
a public nuisance lawsuit

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:10.950
against the hot sauce maker

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.787
after residents began to complain about,

00:10:12.787 --> 00:10:15.380
"Burning eyes, irritated
throats, and headaches."

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:16.550
With other residents claiming

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.630
that they moved outdoor activities indoors

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:21.030
and even would leave their
homes to avoid the stench.

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:23.840
After Sriracha agreed to
install new filtration systems,

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:25.870
the city dropped the suit
in the following year.

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:28.620
But a court is not likely
to stop every annoyance.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:29.840
In defense of a nuisance claim,

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:31.970
a defendant might argue
that the offending activity

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:33.290
complies with zoning laws,

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:35.570
and a court is less
likely to halt an activity

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.390
when the local government has approved it.

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:38.650
Or a defendant might also invoke

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.200
the Coming to the Nuisance defense.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.010
This means that if a defendant can show

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:43.730
that they engaged in this conduct

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:45.800
before the plaintiff
moved to the neighborhood,

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:48.010
the plaintiff was therefore
completely aware of the activity

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:50.420
and chose to live there,
a type of consent.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:52.100
So if you have a very annoying neighbor

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:53.450
and talking it out doesn't work,

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:55.840
just know that you can
always call a lawyer,

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:58.310
because the one thing you
definitely shouldn't do

00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:01.150
is start erecting things out of spite.

00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:02.870
So let's talk about spite,

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:05.260
specifically spite fences, spite houses,

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:07.040
and other spite structures.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.220
Because of certain homeowners,

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:10.670
those with the time,
money, and malicious intent

00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:13.510
to build impractical
structures upon their land

00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:16.560
often do so just to annoy their neighbors.

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:20.610
- All for the express
purpose of taking you down.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.900
- And you better believe that
there is an entire area of law

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:24.870
devoted to such structures.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.990
Now, you might have heard
of a spite fence before,

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:28.420
but there's actually all sorts of things

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:29.960
that you can build out of spite.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:31.640
Now, the law has a specific legal term

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:33.650
to describe any structure
built out of spite,

00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:35.280
and Legal Eagles, I'm going to need you

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:37.170
to be very mature about this

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:41.070
because the very real legal
term is malicious erections.

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:44.970
Hey, hey, there is nothing
funny about malicious erections,

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.400
but please consult your lawyer

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:49.300
if you have a malicious erection
lasting more than 10 hours.

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:51.680
Now, perhaps the most famous spite fence

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:54.210
is the Crocker spite
fence of San Francisco

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:56.540
where a 19th century railroad baron

00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:59.190
built a 40-foot fence
around his neighbor's home

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:01.690
after they refused to
sell him their house,

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:03.820
triggering a 30-year feud.

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:05.990
Enter Charles Crocker, a six foot tall,

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:07.870
300-pound titan of industry

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.670
who made his fortune
overseeing and financing

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:11.950
the construction of the
Central Pacific Railroad.

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:14.200
Crocker had but one humble dream,

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:18.160
building a tiny
12,000-square foot mansion,

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:19.510
buying an entire city block,

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:22.430
and getting San Francisco to
build a residential cable car

00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:24.460
just for the wealthy folks in the area

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:26.420
who were also buying entire city blocks.

00:12:26.420 --> 00:12:28.000
Now, to fully understand the story

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:30.620
which took place during the
Gilded Age of U.S. history,

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:33.870
I need you to imagine a time
where wealth was concentrated

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:35.640
in the hands of the relatively few,

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:38.880
the owners of these big businesses.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:41.110
Laborers toiled for hours and hours a day,

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:43.830
never reaching anything
like what these owners

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:45.110
of these companies had,

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:48.320
all while these ultra
rich few felt emboldened

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:50.700
to blow their money on monuments to ego.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:51.660
- What's all this?

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.240
- Oh, this. Oh, I just came from work.

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:55.800
I'm a secret agent astronaut millionaire.

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:58.690
- Now that you've pictured
such a fantastical scenario

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:01.880
that could never possibly
happen today, we must continue.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:04.330
As this railroad baron bought up the block

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:07.170
and the project neared completion in 1876,

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:10.490
Crocker, the unstoppable force,
met and immovable object,

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:12.140
and his name was Nicholas Yung.

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:14.600
Yung, a German immigrant
who ran a mortuary,

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:18.060
was the sole holdout who
refused to sell his land.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.350
So Crocker decided to torment his neighbor

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:22.240
by building a 40-foot fence,

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:25.740
enclosing the neighbor's house
on three sides out of spite.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:28.360
When Robert Frost wrote, "Good
fences make good neighbors,"

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:31.330
he clearly never had a
neighbor like Charles Crocker.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:32.750
After he built the spite fence,

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:35.820
both sides then took turns
trying to out-spite the other.

00:13:35.820 --> 00:13:38.260
Crocker ordered his workers
to arrange dynamite blasts

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:40.960
so rock debris would pelt the Yung house.

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:43.010
Yung threatened to block Crocker's view

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:44.730
with a skull and crossbones flag

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:46.410
and place a coffin on his roof,

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:47.980
ostensibly to advertise his business,

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:49.810
but mostly to annoy his rich neighbor.

00:13:49.810 --> 00:13:52.960
And after Yung and Crocker
died in 1880 and 1888,

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:55.880
respectively, their heirs
continued this fight.

00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:58.340
Efforts to get the city to tear
down the fence went nowhere

00:13:58.340 --> 00:14:00.490
as the fence technically broke no laws.

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:03.670
Spite fence has only became
illegal in California in 1913.

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:06.840
And after withstanding a
constitutional challenge in 1920,

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:09.530
the modern statute was
finally codified in 1953,

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:12.087
providing that, "Any
fence or other structure

00:14:12.087 --> 00:14:12.987
"in the nature of of a fence

00:14:12.987 --> 00:14:15.377
"unnecessarily exceeding 10 feet in height

00:14:15.377 --> 00:14:17.987
"maliciously erected or
maintained for the purpose

00:14:17.987 --> 00:14:20.927
"of annoying the owner or
occupant of an adjoining property

00:14:20.927 --> 00:14:22.740
"is a private nuisance."

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:26.770
When Yung's widow died in 1902,
the rivalry died with her.

00:14:26.770 --> 00:14:27.950
Their daughter sold the land

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:29.920
to the Crocker descendants in 1904,

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:32.420
and the spite fence was torn down in 1905.

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:34.430
But all this fighting would
turn out to be pointless

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:38.020
as in 1906, the San Francisco earthquake

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:41.310
and related fires burned
down the entire neighborhood.

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:43.650
Apparently, nature is
just as capable as man

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:45.200
of acting out of spite.

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:47.430
And just like spite fences
are impractical structures

00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:49.050
built specifically to annoy,

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:50.650
spite houses are generally built

00:14:50.650 --> 00:14:52.410
with no intention of living there,

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:56.080
like the Plum Island Pink House
in Newbury, Massachusetts.

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:56.970
According to legend,

00:14:56.970 --> 00:14:58.950
a wife agreed to a
divorce from her husband

00:14:58.950 --> 00:15:00.780
on the condition that he build her

00:15:00.780 --> 00:15:03.010
an exact replica of their current home.

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:06.030
But she did not specify where
the house should be built,

00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:07.120
so the husband built the home

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:09.090
in the middle of an isolated salt marsh

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:11.040
that used saltwater for plumbing,

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:12.930
rendering the unit uninhabitable.

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:15.520
And apparently spite runs deep
in the state of Massachusetts

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:18.530
because Boston also boasts
its own famous spite house.

00:15:18.530 --> 00:15:19.363
As the story goes,

00:15:19.363 --> 00:15:21.760
a man returned from
serving in the Civil War

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:24.200
only to find that his brother
had built a large house

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:25.430
on their shared land.

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:27.330
And since the Civil War
adequately prepared him

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:29.160
for brothers being on opposite sides,

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:33.000
the spurned sibling built a
10.4-foot wide skinny house

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:36.030
to block all sunlight and
view of his brother's home.

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:39.180
Now in 2017, the property
was sold to private owners

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:41.660
for $900,000.

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:43.250
But spite structures are not just a thing

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.240
of the distant past.

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:46.530
Back in 2017, Gaver Nichols,

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:49.080
an architect neighbor
in Alexandria, Virginia,

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:51.010
decided to build a new garage two feet

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:53.630
from neighbors' Paul and
Patrice Linehan's property

00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:55.430
to block their first floor window.

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:57.400
The Linehans missed their 15-day period

00:15:57.400 --> 00:15:58.440
to object to the garage

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:00.270
because Nicholas began construction

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:01.490
while they were out of town.

00:16:01.490 --> 00:16:04.140
And the city later concluded
that the spite garage

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:05.920
was not technically illegal.

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:08.540
A year later, the Alexandria
city council amended the code

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:11.030
to now require all structures
to be at least five feet away

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:13.490
from a home with a basement
or first floor window

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:15.510
within three feet of the
shared property line.

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:16.800
But there are so many ways

00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:18.010
that you can spite your neighbors,

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:21.000
as illustrated by one
Michigan man and Vermont man

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:22.750
who individually decided to construct

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:26.130
the ultimate symbol of
spite, a giant middle finger.

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:28.700
In Michigan, strip club
entrepreneur Alan Markovitz

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:30.500
purchased the home next to his ex-wife,

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:32.200
then built a 12-foot high

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:35.680
spotlit bonze middle finger
sculpture in his backyard.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:38.770
Markovitz claims his wife had
an affair with someone he knew

00:16:38.770 --> 00:16:40.657
and felt compelled to spend $7,000

00:16:40.657 --> 00:16:42.950
for the chance to flip them off every day.

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:44.880
Markovitz is no stranger
to making enemies,

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:48.450
having been famously shot
twice, once in the face,

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:50.620
had a mob contract taken out on his life,

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:53.220
and had an ex-girlfriend
drive a Pontiac Fiero

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:54.370
through one of his clubs.

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:56.080
And similarly in Westford, Vermont,

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:58.640
business owner Ted Pelkey
had reached the boiling point

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:00.380
after fighting an 11-year battle

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:02.630
against the town's
development review board,

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:05.220
which had repeatedly denied
his building permit application

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:07.020
for an 8,000-square foot garage.

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:09.770
Mr. Pelkey had previously
expressed his displeasure

00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:11.980
in less than legal ways,

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:14.370
like in 2011 when he
allegedly threatened to shoot

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:17.240
a town official if he
stepped on his property.

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:19.170
- Some people in my situation

00:17:19.170 --> 00:17:20.360
would have probably went and bought a gun,

00:17:20.360 --> 00:17:21.337
but instead I said,

00:17:21.337 --> 00:17:24.247
"Well, I'd rather just
put up a big middle finger

00:17:24.247 --> 00:17:27.550
"in the front yard and just
tell them what I think of them."

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:30.090
- Years later, Mr. Pelkey
found a not quite unique,

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:32.940
but slightly less threatening
way to express his displeasure

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:34.160
with the town officials.

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:37.890
He spent $4,000 on a
700-pound, chainsaw-carved,

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:41.460
wooden middle finger
perched atop a 16-foot pole.

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:43.430
Although one might think
that this would qualify

00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:45.440
as a spite structure or
even a public nuisance

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:47.160
as it flips off the whole town,

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:49.580
the government apparently
could not do anything about it.

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:50.650
That's because the middle finger

00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:52.440
does not advertise a product or service

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:54.930
so it does not fall under
Vermont's billboard law.

00:17:54.930 --> 00:17:57.250
Instead, it likely
qualifies as public artwork

00:17:57.250 --> 00:17:58.910
protected under the First Amendment.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:00.730
The town has fought for
Pelkey to take it down,

00:18:00.730 --> 00:18:02.420
but the middle finger remains.

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:05.510
And it inspired a short
film, "A Very Large Gesture."

